{
  "case_id": "2021-21-147",
  "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0000-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: SARAH M. HARRIS, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner. MICHAEL R. HUSTON, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner. FELICIA H. ELLSWORTH, ESQUIRE, Boston, Massachusetts; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sarah M. Harris",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. HARRIS: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This Court should not expand Bivens for the first time in 40 years. First, Bivens extensions clash with modern precedent. Bivens interpreted federal courts' jurisdiction over federal questions as authorizing courts to fashion new damages actions. Decades of intervening cases reject that premise and remove any doctrinal basis for Bivens extensions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Well, Ms. Harris, the -- when you have -- the Fourth Amendment claim in Bivens is similar to the Fourth Amendment claim here, so why doesn't that foreclose your argument that that's excluded?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael R. Huston (Amicus Curiae for United States)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A straightforward application of this Court's recent Bivens precedents demonstrates"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Felicia H. Ellsworth (Counsel for Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Boule's Fourth Amendment claim is materially indistinguishable from Bivens itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But aren't -- aren't you up against the fact that we have declined to apply or extend Bivens in recent history?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0002-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "this is an unlawful entry without a warrant, and this is excessive force on private property against a U.S. citizen on domestic soil."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: What about Mr. Huston's reference to Canada and the cooperation with Canada, and so this is the border context and it's not just near the border, but there actually is interaction with the Canadian authorities on this kind of activity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the position is that Border Patrol agents writ large should not be subjected to Bivens."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Ellsworth",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "But, if the fact that the agent is conducting a visa check is sufficient to remove the conduct from the ambit of Bivens altogether, that would have extremely broad implications far beyond border patrol."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court found, at the Petition Appendix 65a, that the area where Agent Egbert attempted to question the Turkish guest, where he was standing and where Mr. Boule asked him to leave, was the curtilage of the property, which is protected within the Fourth Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, you know, in those contexts -- take qualified immunity. I -- I -- I -- I kind of get my head around at least what I'm supposed to try to do there, right, is the law clearly established, and I look on the books and see if I can find it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0003-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the Court did, in fact, recognize a new context in Abbasi."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. ELLSWORTH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I would say that the lower courts have not respectfully struggled to -- to quite the same degree with applying the -- the Abbasi framework."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BARRETT",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. Ellsworth, let me ask you a question, the questions following up that Justice Breyer and I were asking about skepticism and given that the Court hasn't recognized a new Bivens claim in decades, given that the Court has said that they're disfavored."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. ELLSWORTH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the Court has already narrowed Bivens substantially."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "9c6212bd4d60d6c0564b9e6879092a7243d7b078c29e34954781a4b5bc3ad4f4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9c6212bd4d60-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On the Fourth Amendment front, how do we -- how should we properly handle invocations of national security by the government?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-21-147",
      "confidence": 0.0,
